<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n905" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγριόω</span></b> , aor.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠγρίωσα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Or.</u>
					616
				</span></i>
			, the act. tenses being mostly supplied by <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγριαίνω, </span>(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄγριος</span>):—<i>makewild</i> or <i>savage,
				provoke</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἣ τῇτεκούσῃ σ᾽
				ἠγρίως ε</span>
			<i>against</i> thy mother, E l.c. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> mostly in 
				Pass.
			, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγριοῦμαι</span>
				Hp.Aër.<i><span class="en">
				4
			</span></i>: impf.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠγριούμην</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>El.</u>
					1031
				</span></i>
			 codd.: aor.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠγριώθην</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Per.</u>
					34
				</span></i>
			: pf.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠγρίωμαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Ph.</u>
					1321
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>IT</u>
				348
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Ra.</u>
				897
			</span></i>:—<i>grow wild</i>; in pf.
			<i>to be wild</i>, properly of plants, countries, etc., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νῆσος ἠγριωμένη τῇ ὕλῃ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Thphr.
					<u>HP</u>
					5.8.2
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>CP</u>
				5.3.6
			</span></i>; of men, <i>to be unkempt</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὡς ἠγρίωσαι διὰ μακρᾶς ἀλουσίας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Or.</u>
					226
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				387
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> in moral sense,
				<i>to be savage, cruel</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠγρίωσαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Ph.</u>
				</span></i>
			l.c., cf. <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>El.</u>
			</span></i>l.c., etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γλῶσσα . .
			ἠγρίωται</span>, of Aeschylus, Ar.l.c.: metaph., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠγριωμένον πέλαγος</span> an
			<i>angrysea</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Pyrrh.</u>
				15
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> Medic.,
				<i>become malignant</i>, of wounds, Hp.l.c.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
